## 6. Relation to Existing Analysis

Andreas and Garcia-Fernandez use an implicit-function theorem to perturb a
Calabi-Yau/stable-bundle starting point to a Strominger solution. That theorem
does not directly apply to the non-Kaehler q79 starting geometry, but it
confirms the stable-bundle full-system strategy. Garcia-Fernandez, Rubio and
Tipler prove that the Strominger deformation and obstruction spaces arise from
an elliptic complex. G3Z uses the corresponding gauge-slice logic but supplies
its own elementary a posteriori contraction proof and does not assume a
Calabi-Yau or transverse starting point.

Primary references:

- B. Andreas and M. Garcia-Fernandez, *Solutions of the Strominger System via
  Stable Bundles on Calabi-Yau Threefolds*,
  https://arxiv.org/abs/1008.1018.
- M. Garcia-Fernandez, R. Rubio and C. Tipler, *Infinitesimal Moduli for the
  Strominger System and Killing Spinors in Generalized Geometry*,
  https://arxiv.org/abs/1503.07562.

